    sample order computes ``L = sum(w_i * rho(t_i - p_i))`` and
    ``L0 = sum(w_i * rho(t_i - q))``. When ``L0`` is non-zero the result
    is ``1.0 - L / L0``; when ``L0`` and ``L`` are both zero the result
    is ``1.0``; when only ``L0`` is zero the result is ``0.0``.

